<p>Use this menu to make settings for covers, slip sheets, or chapter pages.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="front" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Front Cover</span></p>
<p>Prints the first page on a slip sheet or inserts a blank sheet as the 
 front cover.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_FRONTCOVER">Printing Only the First Sheet on a 
 Different Type of Paper</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span></p>
<p>Select the tray containing the paper to use for the front cover.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print Mode:</span></p>
<p>Select one of the options for the cover.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Leave Blank</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">The cover sheet is not printed on. Printing begins 
 on the second sheet.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">One Side</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Only one side of the cover sheet is printed on. 
 If you have specified 2 sided printing, selecting this will ensure only 
 one side of the cover sheet is printed on.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Both Sides</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Both sides of the cover sheet are printed on. This 
 option is available only for 2 sided printing.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type in Bypass Tray...</span></p>
<p>Specify the type of printing medium you want to use when using bypass 
 tray paper as the front cover sheet. Available media types differ depending 
 on the printer you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="back" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Back Cover</span></p>
<p>Prints the last page on a slip sheet or inserts a blank sheet as the 
 back cover.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_BACKCOVER">Printing the Back Cover on a Different 
 Type of Paper</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span></p>
<p>Select the tray containing the paper to use for the back cover.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Depending on the printer you use, the input tray 
 selected for the front cover may be always used for the last sheet. In 
 this case, the <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> list is unavailable.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print Mode:</span></p>
<p>Select one of the options for the back cover.<br/>
Depending on the printer you are using, the available items may vary.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Leave Blank</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">The back cover sheet is not printed on.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print on Back Cover</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints on the back cover sheet.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print on Outer Back Cov.</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints on the back side of the back cover sheet.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type in Bypass Tray...</span></p>
<p>Specify the type of printing medium you want to use when using bypass 
 tray paper as the back cover sheet. Available media types differ depending 
 on the printer you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="slip" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Insert Slip Sheet After Every Page</span></p>
<p>Inserts a separator sheet after every printed sheet.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_SLIPSHEET">Inserting Different Paper between Pages</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span></p>
<p>Select the tray containing the paper to use for the slip sheets.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The slip sheet function is not available if the 
 same input trays are selected for both print pages and slip sheets.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print Mode:</span></p>
<p>Select whether or not to print on slip sheets.<br/>
Depending on the printer you are using, the available items may vary.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Leave Blank</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Inserts a blank sheet as a separator.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print on Slip Sheet</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints on slip sheets.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type in Bypass Tray...</span></p>
<p>Specify the type of printing medium you want to use when using bypass 
 tray paper as the slip sheet. Available media types differ depending on 
 the printer you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="designate" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter</span></p>
<p>You can divide a document into chapters and print the first page of 
 each chapter on different paper. You can also select the print mode for 
 the first page of each chapter. (Designate/Chapter)<br/>
In addition, you can print the selected pages on different paper. (Designated 
 Sheet Print)</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_CHAPTER">Using Designate/Chapter Function</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span></p>
<p>Opens the <span class="Term-Soft">Designate/Chapter Details</span> dialog 
 box where you can configure the detailed settings.</p>
